"\", \"needs_cl\": true, \"lane\": \"T3-REOPEN\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-4-8\"}\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-7-## Headline\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-8-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:9:195 line-items dispositioned = **162 T3-REOPEN findings** + **33 residual (`no-live-star`) rows reconciled within them** + **7 UNRESOLVED cross-cites**, incl. the Herring loop-2 resolution.\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-10-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-11-| action (per finding) | count | keys |\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-14-| **kept-conversion-provenance** → documented S.Ct→U.S. conversion; U.S. pin kept; lake conversion-note | 5 | 5 |\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-15-| **converted** → content interior pin retired to first-page cite; lake stays slip-only; → R12 | 85 | 44 |\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:16:| **converted-sct** (Herring 144, loop-2 ruling) → re-cited to star-verified `129 S. Ct. at 702`; lake re-based; U.S. 144 → R12 | 6 | 1 |\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-17-| **provenanced-no-action** (7 UNRESOLVED) → star page present in cache; not a defect | 7 | 5 |\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-18-| **TOTAL fix rows** | **169** | |\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-22-## Method — canonical per-(opinion,pin) coverage (deterministic)\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-23-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:24:The input `refined_status` is assigned **per finding-row** and is internally inconsistent for the same `(opinion_id, pin)` across pages (e.g. Herring 144 tagged both `start-page-covered` and `no-live-star` on different pages). Star coverage is a fact about `(opinion, pin)`, so coverage was recomputed **directly from the refetch `html_with_citations`** — the artifact P4-12(a) names as the provenance:\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-25-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-26-- Extract visible `*NNN` / `<page-num label=\"NNN\">` star markers per `<opid>.html`.\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-28-- **live-star** ⟺ pin ∈ U.S. run; **start-page** ⟺ pin is the opinion's landing page (first U.S. marker = pin+1); else **convert**.\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-29-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:30:Result: **29 upgrade keys** (28 live-star + 1 start-page = Brendlin 251), **44 convert**, **5 documented-conversion keep**, **1 escalate→converted-sct (Herring 144, loop-2)**.\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-31-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-32-### Reconciliation vs the `refined_status` file — flagged for orchestrator sample-check\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-36-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-37-**(B) 4 refined `start-page-covered` rows REFUTED by the html** (the live pagination is S.Ct-only; no U.S. star run, so the U.S. page is not a verifiable landing page):\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:38:- Herring 144 (fl 28, 94) → **converted-sct** (loop-2 ruling; see below).\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-39-- Los Angeles County v. Rettele 614 (fl 100) → **kept-conversion-provenance** (page documents `127 S. Ct. at 1993–94`, star-verified).\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-40-- Scott v. Harris 386 (fl 115) → **converted** (bare U.S. pin, S.Ct-only markers 1772–1785).\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-54-| Los Angeles County v. Rettele | 550 U.S. 614 | 127 S. Ct. 1993–94 (markers 1990–1994) | pin-1993 |\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-55-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:56:## Herring v. United States 555 U.S. 144 — escalated, then RESOLVED loop-2 (orchestrator ruling)\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-57-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:58:Initially escalated: lake `pin-144` was `star-verified (star_marker \"144\")` from a prior phase with an **unrecorded basis**, but the refetch paginates **S. Ct. only** (129 S. Ct. 697–711), the second-source harvest is empty, and content asserted a bare `555 U.S. at 144` with no on-page documented conversion.\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-59-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-60-**Orchestrator ruling (loop-2):** a prior star-verified state with an unrecorded basis is **not verified** (P2 no-prior-grade); but the refetch **does** star-verify the S. Ct. pagination, so an S. Ct. pinpoint is fully provenanced. → **convert to the documented-S.Ct form.**\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-62-**Derived S. Ct. page = 129 S. Ct. 702** (html evidence): the pinned holding *\"To trigger the exclusionary rule, police conduct must be sufficiently deliberate that exclusion can meaningfully deter it, and sufficiently culpable that such deterrence is worth the price paid by the justice system\"* sits between star markers **`*702`** (offset 28678) and **`*703`** (offset 37031) in `_run/s9/p4/star-refetch/145922.html`; the second quote (`^pin-144a`) is on the same page. This equals 555 U.S. 144.\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-63-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:64:**Applied:** (1) **content** — all 7 U.S.-144 occurrences (the 6 filed findings — case page L55, Collective Knowledge L39/L103, Good-Faith Exception L33/L41/L127 — plus the case-page Sources note L73) re-cited to the star-verified `129 S. Ct. at 702` documented-conversion form (mirrors Rettele; quotes/prose intact). Zero bare `555 U.S. 144` assertions remain. (2) **lake** `pin-144` re-based: `star_marker=\"702\"`, `pinpoint_status` stays `star-verified`, conversion note recording the unrecorded U.S. basis + the S.Ct star evidence. (3) **R12** — Herring added (retired value `555 U.S. 144`, S.Ct rebase `129 S. Ct. 702`). (4) fixes.jsonl 6 rows `escalated → converted-sct` (`loop:2`). Contrast Heien 60 — same shape but with an on-page documented conversion, kept as-is.\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-65-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-66-## The 33 residual (`no-live-star`) rows — reconciled\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-67-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:68:These are **sibling content locations** of pins whose case-page finding got a coverage verdict; the refetch pipeline left the sibling rows unrefined. Recomputed against the html oracle they resolve deterministically: **27 upgraded** (siblings of star-verified pins — e.g. Hudson 594, Grubbs 96/99, Randolph 120, Samson 857, Ryburn 476/477, Brigham 400/404), **4 converted-sct** (Herring 144, loop-2), **1 kept-conversion** (Moore 168 mirror), **1 converted** (Scott 386). No residual left unclassified.\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-69-\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-70-## The 7 UNRESOLVED cross-cites — all PROVENANCED (no defect)\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-93-## Output files\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-94-- `_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-fixes.jsonl` — 169 rows (66 upgraded / 5 kept-conversion / 85 converted / 6 converted-sct / 7 provenanced-no-action).\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md:95:- `_run/s9/p4/out/R12-pin-upgrade-queue.jsonl` — 86 rows (every converted pin + Herring loop-2 rebase: case, cluster_id, retired printed pin, file:line — for re-verification when official U.S. Reports pagination lands).\n_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md-96-- `_run/s9/p4/out/FIX-T3-summary.md` — this file.\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/S8H-B-ledger-sample.jsonl-16-{\"kind\": \"mention\", \"idx\": 140, \"file\": \"content/cases/Anderson v. Creighton.md\", \"line\": 53, \"matched_text\": \"Anderson v. Creighton\", \"action\": \"exempt:heading\", \"method\": \"zone\", \"target\": null, \"check\": \"OK\", \"notes\": [], \"at_recorded_line\": true, \"drift\": false, \"absent\": false}\n_run/s9/p4/out/S8H-B-ledger-sample.jsonl-17-{\"kind\": \"mention\", \"idx\": 150, \"file\": \"content/cases/Andresen v. Maryland.md\", \"line\": 31, \"matched_text\": \"Coolidge v. New Hampshire\", \"action\": \"exempt:frontmatter\", \"method\": \"zone\", \"target\": null, \"check\": \"OK\", \"notes\": [], \"at_recorded_line\": true, \"drift\": false, \"absent\": false}\n_run/s9/p4/out/S8H-B-ledger-sample.jsonl:18:{\"kind\": \"mention\", \"idx\": 160, \"file\": \"content/cases/Arizona v. Evans.md\", \"line\": 31, \"matched_text\": \"Herring v. United States\", \"action