ages), but no pair contains incompatible rule statements, opposite outcomes, conflicting scope claims, or mutually-exclusive boundary sentences. Rule quotes, holdings, and pincite anchors align across homes.\n_run/s9/p4/out/PAIR-P1-summary.md-39-\n_run/s9/p4/out/PAIR-P1-summary.md-40-## Out-of-R6-scope observations (for orchestrator triage — not PAIR-P1 hits)\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/TW-CLAUDE-2-summary.md-19-### Unit 6 EXCLUSIONARY, REMEDIES & STANDING  (10 searches)\n_run/s9/p4/out/TW-CLAUDE-2-summary.md-20-Threads: good-faith SCOTUS; Strieff/attenuation; SCOTUS-2025-term 4A; inevitable-discovery/independent-source;\n_run/s9/p4/out/TW-CLAUDE-2-summary.md:21:standing/REP; Herring/Davis good-faith; +2 caption-confirms (1st Cir 25-1041, Ray/Chatrie); attenuation-circuit.\n_run/s9/p4/out/TW-CLAUDE-2-summary.md-22-- FILED: **United States v. Parkerson** (5th Cir. 2025, trespasser no-REP standing);\n_run/s9/p4/out/TW-CLAUDE-2-summary.md-23-  **United States v. Gonzalez-Arocho** (1st Cir. No. 25-1041 published, good-faith rejected / warrant-scope);\n--\n_run/s9/p4/out/TW-DIFF-findings.jsonl-126-{\"row\": \"p4.candidate.v1\", \"ws\": \"I5\", \"packet\": \"TW-DIFF\", \"class\": \"frontier-unaccounted\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"file\": \"_run/s9/p4/out/codex/TW-confessions.txt\", \"line\": 11, \"assertion_id\": \"\", \"claim\": \"frontier case NOT-ACCOUNTED: United States v. Morgan (U.S. Court of Appeals for the Eleventh Circuit, 2025-07-11, No. 23-11114) absent by name from corpus+lake+S6; doctrine=Vega progeny/Miranda physical fruits/abandonment/deception; class_saturation=SATURATED.\", \"evidence\": \"Absent by name from content/ (docket+reporter grep=0 on ['23-11114']), _overhaul2/lake/cases/ (no own-record docket/cite/distinctive-name), and _run/s6-candidates/* + s6-borderline.md + s6-coverage-ledger.json + s6-fabrications.md (grep=0). found_by=codex-only; unit(s)=['confessions']. class_saturation: SATURATED \\u2014 Miranda/waiver/voluntariness saturated (S6 confessions st