nson-v-glick/\", \"holding\": \"Not every use of force by a custodial officer is a constitutional violation; whether the line is crossed depends on the need for force, the relationship between the need and the amount used, the extent of injury, and whether force was applied in good faith to maintain discipline or maliciously to cause harm — the pre-Graham due-process test for excessive force.\", \"leg\": \"roster\", \"prong\": \"c\", \"basis\": \"D1-flip\", \"homes\": [\"use-of-force-and-liability/Use of Force.md\"], \"roles\": [{\"home\": \"use-of-force-and-liability/Use of Force.md\", \"role\": \"Key\"}], \"primary_home\": \"Use of Force\", \"home_rows\": [{\"home\": \"use-of-force-and-liability/Use of Force.md\", \"role\": \"Key\", \"role_class\": \"key\", \"schema\": \"key\", \"stem\": \"Johnson v. Glick\", \"cite\": \"481 F.2d 1028 (1973)\", \"holding_cell_hint\": \"Not every use of force by a custodial officer is a constitutional violation; whether the line is crossed depends on the need for force, the relationship between the need and the amount used, the extent of injury, and whether force was applied in good faith to maintain discipline or maliciously to cause harm — the pre-Graham due-process test for excessive force.\"}], \"worklist_note\": null, \"page\": \"content/cases/Johnson v. Glick.md\", \"born_status\": \"under_review\", \"lints_run\": [\"LINT-15\", \"LINT-16\", \"LINT-14\"], \"as_of\": \"2026-07-07\", \"ts\": \"2026-07-07\", \"lane\": \"s6-r8-mint\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-4-8\"}\n_run/o2-execute/s6-authored-ledger.jsonl:39:{\"terminal\": \"authored\", \"record_id_before\": \"knight-v-jacobson--778847\", \"record_id_after\": \"Knight v. Jacobson\", \"caption\": \"Knight v. Jacobson\", \"cite\": \"300 F.3d 1272 (2002)\", \"year\": 2002, \"court\": \"11th Cir. 2002\", \"authority_weight\": \"Binding in-circuit — 11th Cir.\", \"opinion_url\": \"https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/778847/arthur-knight-v-jacobson-officer-badge-3359-individual/\", \"holding\": \"Payton's warrant requirement for in-home arrests is not violated when an officer standing outside the home orders a suspect to step outside and then arrests him without a warrant — Payton keeps the officer's body, not his voice, outside the threshold.\", \"leg\": \"roster\", \"prong\": \"a\", \"basis\": \"D1-flip\", \"homes\": [\"seizures/arrests/Arrest in the Home.md\"], \"roles\": [{\"home\": \"seizures/arrests/Arrest in the Home.md\", \"role\": \"Key\"}], \"primary_home\": \"Arrest in the Home\", \"home_rows\": [{\"home\": \"seizures/arrests/Arrest in the Home.md\", \"role\": \"Key\", \"role_class\": \"key\", \"schema\": \"key\", \"stem\": \"Knight v. Jacobson\", \"cite\": \"300 F.3d 1272 (2002)\", \"holding_cell_hint\": \"Payton's warrant requirement for in-home arrests is not violated when an officer standing outside the home orders a suspect to step outside and then arrests him without a warrant — Payton keeps the officer's body, not his voice, outside the threshold.\"}], \"worklist_note\": null, \"page\": \"content/cases/Knight v. Jacobson.md\", \"born_status\": \"under_review\", \"lints_run\": [\"LINT-15\", \"LINT-16\", \"LINT-14\"], \"as_of\": \"2026-07-07\", \"ts\": \"2026-07-07\", \"lane\": \"s6-r8-mint\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-4-8\"}\n_run/o2-execute/s6-authored-ledger.jsonl:40:{\"terminal\": \"authored\", \"record_id_before\": \"laduke-v-nelson--452994\", \"record_id_after\": \"LaDuke v. Nelson\", \"caption\": \"LaDuke v. Nelson\", \"cite\": \"762 F.2d 1318 (1985)\", \"year\": 1985, \"court\": \"9th Cir.\", \"authority_weight\": \"Binding in-circuit — 9th Cir.\", \"opinion_url\": \"https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/452994/charles-laduke-v-alan-c-nelson-etc/\", \"holding\": \"Migrant farmworkers' dwellings retain their occupants' reasonable expectations of privacy, so the INS may not conduct warrantless 'area control' entries of farm housing to search or arrest absent consent or probable cause; the Ninth Circuit affirmed a class inj