{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":1,\"target\":\"index.md rule-callout accuracy\",\"verdict\":\"REFUTE\",\"basis\":\"The categorical text omits applicability limits, and its fruits proposition is not supported by Weeks *393, Mapp *655, or Calandra *348; Calandra discusses fruits on *347.\"}\n{\"item\":1,\"target\":\"Weeks, 232 U.S. 383, 393\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Cache 98094.txt has marker *393 and explains that permitting unlawfully seized letters to be held and used as evidence would make the Fourth Amendment valueless.\"}\n{\"item\":1,\"target\":\"Mapp, 367 U.S. 643, 655\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Cache 106285.txt has marker *655 and expressly holds unconstitutionally seized evidence inadmissible in state court.\"}\n{\"item\":1,\"target\":\"Calandra, 414 U.S. 338, 348\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Cache 108898.txt at *348 calls exclusion a judicially created remedy safeguarding Fourth Amendment rights through deterrence, not a personal constitutional right.\"}\n{\"item\":1,\"target\":\"index.md callout format\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Matches sibling structure exactly: '> [!rule] Black-letter rule', quoted body, then a block anchor line.\"}\n{\"item\":2,\"target\":\"seven Herring content conversions\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"The seven edits are case page rule/source, Collective Knowledge prose/source, and Good-Faith prose/bullet/source. Refetch 145922.html places the relevant recordkeeping discussion and quoted culpability holding after *702 and before *703.\"}\n{\"item\":2,\"target\":\"remaining '555 U.S. at 144' in content\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Repository-wide content search returned zero occurrences, including broader searches for Herring citations pairing 555 U.S. 135 with interior 144.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 21: Florida v. Powell converted pin 60\",\"verdict\":\"REFUTE\",\"basis\":\"Rule quote and prose were preserved and the inline cite became 559 U.S. 50, but the same page still asserts 'pinpoints: 60, 62' in Sources.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 38: Missouri v. McNeely converted pin 156\",\"verdict\":\"REFUTE\",\"basis\":\"Rule quote and prose were preserved and the inline cite became 569 U.S. 141, but Sources still expressly asserts pinpoint 156.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 72: Heien v. North Carolina converted pin 61\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Traffic Stops retains the mistake-of-law proposition while replacing 574 U.S. at 61 with 574 U.S. 54; no pin 61 remains on that page.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 106: Messerschmidt v. Millender converted pin 547\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Franks Challenges preserves the prose and replaces 565 U.S. 535, 547 with 565 U.S. 535 in both prose and Sources; no 547 assertion remains.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 157: Riley v. California converted pin 387\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"SIA Cell Phones preserves the physical-handset quotation and surrounding prose while retiring all 387 citations to 573 U.S. 373, including Sources.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 4: Brigham City upgraded pin 400\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Refetch 145654.html contains an explicit U.S.-reporter star marker *400.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 55: United States v. Grubbs upgraded pin 96\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Refetch 145670.html contains an explicit U.S.-reporter star marker *96.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 89: Brendlin v. California upgraded pin 251\",\"verdict\":\"REFUTE\",\"basis\":\"Refetch 145712.html contains no *251 marker; its first explicit U.S.-reporter star marker is *252, so the claimed star page does not itself exist in the HTML.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 123: Fernandez v. California upgraded pin 303\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Refetch 9798884.html contains page-label data-label='303' rendered as *303.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"target\":\"FIX-T3 row 140: Ryburn v. Huff upgraded pin 477\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Refetch 622303.html contains an explicit star-page marker *477.\"}\n{\"item\":4,\"target\":\"Horton v. California lake promotion\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Record status is verified_identity; schema-sanctioned provenance.warnings records the P4-10 promotion, and PROMO-identity-fetch.json independently matches Horton, 496 U.S. 128, and 1990-06-04.\"}\n{\"item\":4,\"target\":\"Imbler v. Pachtman lake promotion and pin *431\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Status is verified_identity with promotion evidence in provenance.warnings and pinpoint provenance in field_provenance.pinpoints; cache 9426281.txt places the stored holding after marker *431.\"}\n{\"item\":4,\"target\":\"Riley v. California lake promotion\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Status is verified_identity; provenance.warnings records P4-10 identity confirmation and the CL-selected 134 S. Ct. 2473 identity is consistent with the record and ruling.\"}\n{\"item\":4,\"target\":\"Heien v. North Carolina lake promotion and 574 U.S. 54 placement\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Status is verified_identity with promotion/cite-selector evidence in provenance.warnings; 574 U.S. 54 appears in citations.parallel and citations.all with whitelist source text, not as the selected official cite.\"}\n{\"item\":4,\"target\":\"Arizona v. Youngblood lake promotion and date\",\"verdict\":\"CONFIRM\",\"basis\":\"Status is verified_identity with promotion/date evidence in provenance.warnings; identity.date_decided is 1988-11-29 and identity.year is 1988.\"}\n{\"item\":5,\"target\":\"Private and Foreign Searches hash-split edit\",\"verdict\":\"REFUTE\",\"basis\":\"Lowers and Brillhart propositions match their stubs, no page-less wikilinks were introduced, and 'The Supreme Court has not resolved it' remains; however, both new bullets use unsanctioned labels 'Binding in-circuit (Nth Cir.